tional Attributes Name class( flop_recorder_type ), intent(inout) :: self Source Code type :: flop_recorder_type !! the flop recorder type simply contains a flop count !! this should be the largest possible integer in the planet !! currently this will overflow for zetta flops private integer ( int64 ) :: flop_count = 0_int64 contains procedure , non_overridable :: add => add_flops procedure , non_overridable :: get => get_flops procedure , non_overridable :: reset => reset_flop_counter end type flop_recorder_type","tags":"","url":"type/flop_recorder_type.html"},{"title":"csr_t – PIC ","text":"type, public :: csr_t Compressed sparse row matrix with real(dp) values. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), public, allocatable :: col_idx (:) Column index of every stored entry, ascending within each row integer(kind=default_int), public :: ncol = 0 Number of columns; prefer the n_cols accessor when reading integer(kind=default_int), public :: nrow = 0 Number of rows; prefer the n_rows accessor when reading integer(kind=default_int), public, allocatable :: row_ptr (:) Row start offsets, size nrow + 1 , one-based real(kind=dp), public, allocatable :: values (:) Value of every stored entry, parallel to col_idx Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: build_from_coo => csr_build_from_coo private  subroutine csr_build_from_coo (self, n_rows, n_cols, rows, cols, vals, err) Build the matrix from coordinate (COO) triplets. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n_rows Number of rows of the assembled matrix integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n_cols Number of columns of the assembled matrix integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: rows (:) Row coordinate of each triplet integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: cols (:) Column coordinate of each triplet real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: vals (:) Value of each triplet type( error_t ), intent(out)