_t – PIC ","text":"type, public :: soa_extent_t Size and capacity bookkeeping for one SoA container. Held as a component of the container rather than inherited from a base\ntype: PIC targets compilers whose support for type extension plus\ntype-bound generics is uneven, and composition costs nothing here. Inherited by type~~soa_extent_t~~InheritedByGraph type~soa_extent_t soa_extent_t type~particle_soa_t particle_soa_t type~particle_soa_t->type~soa_extent_t extent Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Type Type This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a derived type to the parent type which it\nextends. Dashed arrows point from a derived type to the other\ntypes it contains as a components, with a label listing the name(s) of\nsaid component(s). Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), public :: capacity = 0 Allocated length of every field array. integer(kind=default_int), public :: used = 0 Number of live elements. This is what size() returns. Source Code type :: soa_extent_t !! Size and capacity bookkeeping for one SoA container. !! !! Held as a component of the container rather than inherited from a base !! type: PIC targets compilers whose support for type extension plus !! type-bound generics is uneven, and composition costs nothing here. integer ( default_int ) :: used = 0 !! Number of live elements. This is what `size()` returns. integer ( default_int ) :: capacity = 0 !! Allocated length of every field array. end type soa_extent_t","tags":"","url":"type/soa_extent_t.html"},{"title":"array_hash64_t – PIC ","text":"type, public :: array_hash64_t A streaming 64-bit FNV-1a accumulator over array state. A freshly declared array_hash64_t is already seeded with ARRAY_HASH64_OFFSET_BASIS , so no explicit initialisation call is\nneeded. Feed it with update , read it with digest , and start over\nwith reset . Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), private :: nbytes = 0_int64 Number of encoded bytes consumed so far. Fixed-width int64 so\nthat hashing more than 2 GiB of state cannot overflow the counter\nin a default_int == int32 build. integer(kind=int64), private :: state = ARRAY_HASH64_OFFSET_BASIS Running hash. Fixed-width int64 , because FNV-1a is defined\nmodulo 2**64. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: bytes_hashed => array_hash64_bytes_hashed private pure function array_hash64_bytes_hashed (this) result(nbytes) Number of encoded bytes consumed so far. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( array_hash64_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) procedure, public :: digest => array_hash64_digest private pure function array_hash64_digest (this) result(hash_value) The digest of everything fed in so far. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( array_hash64_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=int64) procedure, public :: reset => array_hash64_reset private pure subroutine array_hash64_reset (this, seed) Return the accumulator to its initial state. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( array_hash64_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer(kind=int64), intent(in), optional :: seed Starting hash value; defaults to ARRAY_HASH64_OFFSET_BASIS . generic, public :: update => update64_int8_0 , update64_int8_1 , update64_int8_2 , update64_int8_3 , update64_int16_0 , update64_int16_1 , update64_int16_2 , update64_int16_3 , update64_int32_0 , update64_int32_1 , update64_int32_2 , update64_int32_3 , update64_int64_0 , update64_int64_1 , update64_int64_2 , update64_int64_3 , update64_rsp_0 , update64_rsp_1 , update64_rsp_2 , update64_rsp_3 , update64_rdp_0 , update64_rdp_1 , update64_rdp_2 , update64_rdp_3 , update64_csp_0 , update64_csp_1 , update64_csp_2 , update64_csp_3 , update64_cdp_0 