aphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), private :: bound integer(kind=int64), private :: candidate integer(kind=int64), private :: mask Source Code function pcg32_next_below ( gen , n , error ) result ( r ) !! Uniform integer in [0, n) from a PCG32 generator. Each attempt consumes !! two 32-bit outputs, so the stream stays word aligned no matter how many !! rejections occur. type ( pcg32_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gen integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: n type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ), optional :: error integer ( default_int ) :: r integer ( int64 ) :: bound , mask , candidate r = 0_default_int if ( n <= 0_default_int ) then if ( present ( error )) then call error % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"pic_rng: next_below requires n > 0\" ) end if return end if if ( n == 1_default_int ) return bound = int ( n , int64 ) mask = rejection_mask ( bound ) do candidate = iand ( gen % next_u64 (), mask ) if ( candidate < bound ) exit end do r = int ( candidate , default_int ) end function pcg32_next_below","tags":"","url":"proc/pcg32_next_below.html"},{"title":"pcg32_next_real_dp – PIC","text":"private  function pcg32_next_real_dp(gen) result(r) Uniform real(dp) in [0, 1) from a PCG32 generator. Consumes two\n32-bit outputs. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( pcg32_t ), intent(inout) :: gen Return Value real(kind=dp) Calls proc~~pcg32_next_real_dp~~CallsGraph proc~pcg32_next_real_dp pcg32_next_real_dp proc~pcg32_next_u64 pcg32_t%pcg32_next_u64 proc~pcg32_next_real_dp->proc~pcg32_next_u64 proc~real_from_word real_from_word proc~pcg32_next_real_dp->proc~real_from_word proc~pcg32_step pcg32_step proc~pcg32_next_u64->proc~pcg32_step proc~rotate_right32 rotate_right32 proc~pcg32_step->proc~rotate_right32 proc~u64_add u64_add proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_add proc~u64_mul u64_mul proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_mul proc~u64_shr u64_shr proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_shr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Grap