itmix64_next_normal_dp->interface~next_real_dp interface~next_exponential_dp next_exponential_dp interface~next_exponential_dp->proc~pcg32_next_exponential_dp interface~next_exponential_dp->proc~splitmix64_next_exponential_dp interface~next_normal_dp next_normal_dp interface~next_normal_dp->proc~pcg32_next_normal_dp interface~next_normal_dp->proc~splitmix64_next_normal_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code function splitmix64_next_u64 ( self ) result ( r ) !! Full 64-bit random word. For SplitMix64 this is simply `next`; it !! exists so that both engines present the same interface to the shared !! real and bounded-integer conversions. class ( splitmix64_t ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer ( int64 ) :: r r = self % next () end function splitmix64_next_u64","tags":"","url":"proc/splitmix64_next_u64.html"},{"title":"stream_seed – PIC","text":"private pure function stream_seed(master_seed, stream_id) result(s) Deterministic seed for stream_id under master_seed . mix64 is applied to the master seed, the stream id is spread over the\nwhole word by multiplying stream_id + 1 by the golden-ratio constant,\nthe two are combined with ieor , and the result is mixed once more.\nAdding one to the id keeps stream 0 from collapsing the multiplication\nto zero. Only bit-model and modular arithmetic is used, so the mapping\nis identical on every compiler. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: master_seed integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: stream_id Return Value integer(kind=int64) Calls proc~~stream_seed~~CallsGraph proc~stream_seed stream_seed proc~mix64 mix64 proc~stream_seed->proc~mix64 proc~u64_add u64_add proc~stream_seed->proc~u64_add proc~u64_mul u64_mul proc~stream_seed->proc~u64_mul proc~mix64->proc~u64_mul proc~u64_shr u64_shr proc~mix64->proc~u64_shr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~stream_seed~~CalledByGraph proc~stream_seed stream_seed proc~stream_for_pcg32 stream_for_pcg32 proc~stream_for_pcg32->proc~stream_seed proc~stream_for_splitmix64 stream_for_splitmix64 proc~stream_for_splitmix64->proc~stream_seed interface~stream_for stream_for interface~stream_for->proc~stream_for_pcg32 interface~stream_for->proc~stream_for_splitmix64 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function stream_seed ( master_seed , stream_id ) result ( s ) !! Deterministic seed for `stream_id` under `master_seed`. !! !! `mix64` is applied to the master seed, the stream id is spread over the !! whole word by multiplying `stream_id + 1` by the golden-ratio constant, !! the two are combined with `ieor`, and the result is mixed once more. !! Adding one to the id keeps stream 0 from collapsing the multiplication !! to zero. Only bit-model and modular arithmetic is used, so the mapping !! is identical on every compiler. integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: master_seed integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: stream_id integer ( int64 ) :: s s = mix64 ( ieor ( mix64 ( master_seed ), & u64_mul ( u64_add ( int ( stream_id , int64 ), 1_int64 ), GOLDEN_GAMMA ))) end function stream_seed","tags":"","url":"proc/stream_seed.html"},{"title":"u32_to_int32 – PIC","text":"private pure function u32_to_int32(u) result(r) Reinterpret an unsigned 32-bit value held in [0, 2**32) as the signed int32 with the same bit pattern. Done arithmetically rather than with transfer , and without ever passing an out-of-range value to int . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: u Return Value integer(kind=int32) Called by proc~~u32_to_int32~~CalledByGraph proc~u32_to_int32 u32_to_int32 proc~pcg32_next pcg32_t%pcg32_next proc~pcg32_next->proc~u32_to_int32 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function u32_to_int32 ( u ) result ( r ) !! Reinterpret an unsigned 32-bit value held in [0, 2**32) as the signed !! `int32` with the same bit pattern. Done arithmetically rather than with !! `transfer`, and without ever passing an out-of-range value to `int`. integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: u integer ( int32 ) :: r if ( u >= TWO_TO_31 ) then r = int ( u - TWO_TO_32 , int32 ) else r = int ( u , int32 ) end if end function u32_to_int32","tags":"","url":"proc/u32_to_int32.html"},{"title":"pcg32_seed – PIC","text":"private  subroutine pcg32_seed(self, state, seq) Seed the generator, following the reference pcg32_srandom_r : the\nstream selector is shifted left and forced odd to become the LCG\nincrement, then the state is warmed up, offset by the requested state\nand warmed up again. Type Bound pcg32_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( pcg32_t ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: state integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: seq Calls proc~~pcg32_seed~~CallsGraph proc~pcg32_seed pcg32_t%pcg32_seed proc~pcg32_step pcg32_step proc~pcg32_seed->proc~pcg32_step proc~u64_add u64_add proc~pcg32_seed->proc~u64_add proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_add proc~rotate_right32 rotate_right32 proc~pcg32_step->proc~rotate_right32 proc~u64_mul u64_mul proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_mul proc~u64_shr u64_shr proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_shr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), private :: discard Source Code subroutine pcg32_seed ( self , state , seq ) !! Seed the generator, following the reference `pcg32_srandom_r`: the !! stream selector is shifted left and forced odd to become the LCG !! increment, then the state is warmed up, offset by the requested state !! and warmed up again. class ( pcg32_t ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: state integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: seq integer ( int64 ) :: discard self % increment = ior ( ishft ( seq , 1 ), 1_int64 ) self % state = 0_int64 discard = pcg32_step ( self ) self % state = u64_add ( self % state , state ) discard = pcg32_step ( self ) end subroutine pcg32_seed","tags":"","url":"proc/pcg32_seed.html"},{"title":"splitmix64_seed – PIC","text":"private  subroutine splitmix64_seed(self, s) Set the generator state. Any 64-bit value is a valid seed, including\nzero: SplitMix64 has no degenerate state. Type Bound splitmix64_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( splitmix64_t ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: s Called by proc~~splitmix64_seed~~CalledByGraph proc~splitmix64_seed splitmix64_t%splitmix64_seed proc~stream_for_pcg32 stream_for_pcg32 proc~stream_for_pcg32->proc~splitmix64_seed proc~stream_for_splitmix64 stream_for_splitmix64 proc~stream_for_splitmix64->proc~splitmix64_seed interface~stream_for stream_for interface~stream_for->proc~stream_for_pcg32 interface~stream_for->proc~stream_for_splitmix64 Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine splitmix64_seed ( self , s ) !! Set the generator state. Any 64-bit value is a valid seed, including !! zero: SplitMix64 has no degenerate state. class ( splitmix64_t ), intent ( inout ) :: self integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: s self % state = s end subroutine splitmix64_seed","tags":"","url":"proc/splitmix64_seed.html"},{"title":"stream_for_pcg32 – PIC","text":"private  subroutine stream_for_pcg32(master_seed, stream_id, gen) Build the PCG32 generator belonging to stream_id . The derived seed\ndrives a local SplitMix64 which supplies both the LCG state and the\nstream selector. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: master_seed integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: stream_id type( pcg32_t ), intent(out) :: gen Calls proc~~stream_for_pcg32~~CallsGraph proc~stream_for_pcg32 stream_for_pcg32 proc~splitmix64_next splitmix64_t%splitmix64_next proc~stream_for_pcg32->proc~splitmix64_next proc~splitmix64_seed splitmix64_t%splitmix64_seed proc~stream_for_pcg32->proc~splitmix64_seed proc~stream_seed stream_seed proc~stream_for_pcg32->proc~stream_seed proc~mix64 mix64 proc~splitmix64_next->proc~mix64 proc~u64_add u64_add proc~splitmix64_next->proc~u64_add proc~stream_seed->proc~mix64 proc~stream_seed->proc~u64_add proc~u64_mul u64_mul proc~stream_seed->proc~u64_mul proc~mix64->proc~u64_mul proc~u64_shr