ing: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Module Procedures private elemental function clamp_int32 (x, lo, hi) result(y) Clamp an integer(int32) value to [lo, hi] . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: x integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: lo integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: hi Return Value integer(kind=int32) private elemental function clamp_int64 (x, lo, hi) result(y) Clamp an integer(int64) value to [lo, hi] . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: x integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: lo integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: hi Return Value integer(kind=int64) private elemental function clamp_sp (x, lo, hi) result(y) Clamp a real(sp) value to [lo, hi] . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: x real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: lo real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: hi Return Value real(kind=sp) private elemental function clamp_dp (x, lo, hi) result(y) Clamp a real(dp) value to [lo, hi] . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: x real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: lo real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: hi Return Value real(kind=dp)","tags":"","url":"interface/clamp.html"},{"title":"is_close – PIC","text":"public interface is_close Test two floating-point values for approximate equality. Returns .true. when abs(a - b) <= max(rtol*max(abs(a), abs(b)), atol) .\nThe relative tolerance rtol defaults to sqrt(epsilon) for the\nworking kind and the absolute tolerance atol defaults to 0 ; both\nare optional. Supported kinds are real(sp) and real(dp).\nUsage: flag = is_close(a, b [, rtol] [, atol]) Calls interface~~is_close~~CallsGraph interface~is_close is_close proc~is_close_dp is_close_dp interface~is_close->proc~is_close_dp proc~is_close_sp is_close_sp interface~is_close->proc~is_close_sp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Module Procedures private elemental function is_close_sp (a, b, rtol, atol) result(flag) Approximate equality for real(sp) values. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: a real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: b real(kind=sp), intent(in), optional :: rtol real(kind=sp), intent(in), optional :: atol Return Value logical private elemental function is_close_dp (a, b, rtol, atol) result(flag) Approximate equality for real(dp) values. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: a real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: b real(kind=dp), intent(in), optional :: rtol real(kind=dp), intent(in), optional :: atol Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface/is_close.html"},{"title":"is_in_range – PIC","text":"public interface is_in_range Test whether a value lies within the inclusive range [lo, hi] . Returns .true. when lo <= x .and. 