nd=sp), intent(in) :: lo real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: hi Return Value logical private elemental function is_in_range_dp (x, lo, hi) result(flag) Inclusive range test for real(dp). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: x real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: lo real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: hi Return Value logical","tags":"","url":"interface/is_in_range.html"},{"title":"host_is_little_endian – PIC","text":"public pure function host_is_little_endian() result(is_little) Report whether the running machine stores the least significant byte\nof an integer first. The probe is a transfer between two integer kinds, int8 to int32 . A transfer between a real and an integer kind is\ndeliberately avoided here: it is the construct whose behaviour is\nleast dependable across nvfortran and LFortran, and there is no reason\nto risk it when an integer only probe answers the same question.\nArithmetic alone, iand or ishft , cannot answer it at all, since\nthose operate on values rather than on the storage order of the bytes. Arguments None Return Value logical Source Code pure function host_is_little_endian () result ( is_little ) !! Report whether the running machine stores the least significant byte !! of an integer first. !! !! The probe is a `transfer` between two *integer* kinds, `int8` to !! `int32`. A `transfer` between a real and an integer kind is !! deliberately avoided here: it is the construct whose behaviour is !! least dependable across nvfortran and LFortran, and there is no reason !! to risk it when an integer only probe answers the same question. !! Arithmetic alone, `iand` or `ishft`, cannot answer it at all, since !! those operate on values rather than on the storage order of the bytes. logical :: is_little is_little = ( transfer ([ 1_int8 , 0_int8 , 0_int8 , 0_int8 ], 0_int32 ) == 1_int32 ) end function host_is_little_endian","tags":"","url":"proc/host_is_little_endian.html"},{"title":"record_bytes – PIC","text":"public pure function record_bytes(tag, count) result(nbytes) Total on disk size of a record, including its 12 byte record header. Returns -1 when the tag is unknown or the count is negative. Useful to\nsize a file up front, and used by the test suite to pin the format. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: tag One of the PIC_TAG_* constants. integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: count Number of elements in the record. Return Value integer(kind=int64) Calls proc~~record_bytes~~CallsGraph proc~record_bytes record_bytes proc~element_bytes element_bytes proc~record_bytes->proc~element_bytes Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~record_bytes~~CalledByGraph proc~record_bytes record_bytes proc~soa_stream_bytes soa_stream_bytes proc~soa_stream_bytes->proc~record_bytes proc~particle_soa_serialized_bytes particle_soa_t%particle_soa_serialized_bytes proc~particle_soa_serialized_bytes->proc~soa_stream_bytes Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=int64), private :: esz Source Code pure function record_bytes ( tag , count ) result ( nbytes ) !! Total on disk size of a record, including its 12 byte record header. !! !! Returns -1 when the tag is unknown or the count is negative. Useful to !! size a file up front, and used by the test suite to pin the format. integer ( int32 ), intent ( in ) :: tag !! One of the `PIC_TAG_*` constants. integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: count !! Number of elements in the record. integer ( int64 ) :: nbytes integer ( int64 ) :: esz esz = element_bytes ( tag ) if ( esz < 0_int64 . or . count < 0_int64 ) then nbytes = - 1_int64 else nbytes = PIC_RECORD_HEADER_BYTES + count * esz end if end function record_bytes","tags":"","url":"proc/record_bytes.html"},{"title":"bits_to_real_dp – PIC","text":"private pure function bits_to_real_dp(bits) result(x) Reinterpret the bit pattern of an int64 as a real(dp) .\nSee bits_to_real_sp for why this is confined to the swapped path. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: bits Return Value real(kind=dp) Called by proc~~bits_to_real_dp~~CalledByGraph proc~bits_to_real_dp bits_to_real_dp proc~read_real_dp_array read_real_dp_array proc~read_real_dp_array->proc~bits_to_real_dp interface~read_array read_array interface~read_array->proc~read_real_dp_array proc~soa_read_int32_field soa_read_int32_field proc~soa_read_int32_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_int64_field soa_read_int64_field proc~soa_read_int64_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_logical_field soa_read_logical_field proc~soa_read_logical_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_prologue soa_read_prologue p