s real(sp) straight from the stream and never reinterprets\nanything, which keeps the overwhelmingly common case entirely free of\nany real/integer transfer . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: bits Return Value real(kind=sp) Called by proc~~bits_to_real_sp~~CalledByGraph proc~bits_to_real_sp bits_to_real_sp proc~read_real_sp_array read_real_sp_array proc~read_real_sp_array->proc~bits_to_real_sp interface~read_array read_array interface~read_array->proc~read_real_sp_array proc~soa_read_int32_field soa_read_int32_field proc~soa_read_int32_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_int64_field soa_read_int64_field proc~soa_read_int64_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_logical_field soa_read_logical_field proc~soa_read_logical_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_prologue soa_read_prologue proc~soa_read_prologue->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_real_dp_field soa_read_real_dp_field proc~soa_read_real_dp_field->interface~read_array proc~soa_read_real_sp_field soa_read_real_sp_field proc~soa_read_real_sp_field->interface~read_array interface~soa_read_field soa_read_field interface~soa_read_field->proc~soa_read_int32_field interface~soa_read_field->proc~soa_read_int64_field interface~soa_read_field->proc~soa_read_logical_field interface~soa_read_field->proc~soa_read_real_dp_field interface~soa_read_field->proc~soa_read_real_sp_field proc~particle_soa_deserialize particle_soa_t%particle_soa_deserialize proc~particle_soa_deserialize->proc~soa_read_prologue proc~particle_soa_deserialize->interface~soa_read_field Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function bits_to_real_sp ( bits ) result ( x ) !! Reinterpret the bit pattern of an `int32` as a `real(sp)`. !! !! Only ever reached on the foreign endian read path. The native path !! reads `real(sp)` straight from the stream and never reinterprets !! anything, which keeps the overwhelmingly common case entirely free of !! any real/integer `transfer`. integer ( int32 ), intent ( in ) :: bits real ( sp ) :: x x = transfer ( bits , 0.0_sp ) end function bits_to_real_sp","tags":"","url":"proc/bits_to_real_sp.html"},{"title":"bswap_int32 – PIC","text":"private pure function bswap_int32(x) result(y) Reverse the four bytes of an int32 . Written with ibits / ishft using only non-negative shift counts. ishft with a negative count is avoided because the compilers this\nproject targets have historically disagreed about it, and shiftr is\nFortran 2008 which is more than this needs to assume. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: x Return Value integer(kind=int32) Called by proc~~bswap_int32~~CalledByGraph proc~bswap_int32 bswap_int32 proc~read_header read_header proc~read_header->proc~bswap_int32 proc~read_int32_array read_int32_array proc~read_int32_array->proc~bswap_int32 proc~read_record_header read_record_header proc~read_int32_array->proc~read_record_header proc~read_real_sp_array read_real_sp_array proc~read_real_sp_array->proc~bswap_int32 proc~read_real_sp_array->proc~read_record_header proc~read_record_header->proc~bswap_int32 interface~read_array read_array interface~read_array->proc~read_int32_array interface~read_array->proc~read_real_sp_array proc~read_char_record read_char_record interface~read_array->proc~read_char_record proc~read_in