nction pcg32_next_bernoulli_ppm ( gen , ppm ) result ( r ) !! True with probability `ppm` in a million, from a pcg32_t generator. type ( pcg32_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gen !! Generator, advanced by the draw unless `ppm` is 0 or `PPM_ONE`. integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: ppm !! Probability in parts per million, clamped to `[0, PPM_ONE]`. logical :: r integer ( default_int ) :: clamped clamped = max ( 0_default_int , min ( PPM_ONE , ppm )) if ( clamped == 0_default_int ) then r = . false . return end if if ( clamped == PPM_ONE ) then r = . true . return end if r = pcg32_uniform_below ( gen , int ( PPM_ONE , int64 ) - 1_int64 ) < int ( clamped , int64 ) end function pcg32_next_bernoulli_ppm","tags":"","url":"proc/pcg32_next_bernoulli_ppm.html"},{"title":"pcg32_next_exponential_int – PIC","text":"private  function pcg32_next_exponential_int(gen, mean, err) result(r) Exponential integer with the given mean, from a pcg32_t generator. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( pcg32_t ), intent(inout) :: gen Generator, advanced by one draw, or more in the tail. integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: mean Mean of the distribution, in [0, EXPONENTIAL_MAX_MEAN] . type( error_t ), intent(inout), optional :: err Set to ERROR_VALIDATION when mean is out of range. Return Value integer(kind=int64) Calls proc~~pcg32_next_exponential_int~~CallsGraph proc~pcg32_next_exponential_int pcg32_next_exponential_int proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~pcg32_next_exponential_int->proc~error_set proc~pcg32_next_u64 pcg32_t%pcg32_next_u64 proc~pcg32_next_exponential_int->proc~pcg32_next_u64 proc~scale_by_mean scale_by_mean proc~pcg32_next_exponential_int->proc~scale_by_mean proc~u64_shr u64_shr proc~pcg32_next_exponential_int->proc~u64_shr proc~pcg32_step pcg32_step proc~pcg32_next_u64->proc~pcg32_step proc~scale_by_mean->proc~u64_shr proc~pcg32_step->proc~u64_shr proc~rotate_right32 rotate_right32 proc~pcg32_step->proc~rotate_right32 proc~u64_add u64_add proc~pcg32_step->proc