eger(kind=int64), private :: window Source Code function splitmix64_next_poisson_int ( gen , mean_milli , err ) result ( r ) !! Poisson count with mean `mean_milli/1000`, from a splitmix64_t generator. type ( splitmix64_t ), intent ( inout ) :: gen !! Generator, advanced once per inter-arrival drawn. integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: mean_milli !! A thousand times the mean, in `[0, POISSON_MAX_MEAN_MILLI]`. type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ), optional :: err !! Set to `ERROR_VALIDATION` when `mean_milli` is out of range. integer ( int32 ) :: r integer ( int64 ) :: gap_mean , window , elapsed r = 0_int32 if ( mean_milli < 0_default_int . or . mean_milli > POISSON_MAX_MEAN_MILLI ) then if ( present ( err )) then call err % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , & \"pic_random_dist: next_poisson_int mean_milli out of range\" ) end if return end if if ( mean_milli == 0_default_int ) return ! Mean gap between arrivals, in window ticks: window / (mean_milli/1000). ! That division truncates, so the gap actually used is a little short of ! the one asked for, and the count over a fixed window comes out high -- ! by up to 0.048%, worst at mean_milli = 999596. ! ! Fixing the gap and deriving the window from it instead turns that ! round-off to the sampler's advantage: whatever gap the truncation ! landed on, the window is the one for which that gap is exactly right. ! The residual is the truncation of the window itself, under 1e-6 ! relative. gap_mean = ( POISSON_WINDOW * 1000_int64 ) / int ( mean_milli , int64 ) window = ( gap_mean * int ( mean_milli , int64 )) / 1000_int64 elapsed = 0_int64 do elapsed = elapsed + splitmix64_next_exponential_int ( gen , gap_mean ) if ( elapsed > window ) exit r = r + 1_int32 end do end function splitmix64_next_poisson_int","tags":"","url":"proc/splitmix64_next_poisson_int.html"},{"title":"splitmix64_next_range – PIC","text":"private  function splitmix64_next_range(gen, lo, hi, err) result(r) Uniform integer in [lo, hi] from a splitmix64_t generator