n_milli A thousand times the mean, in [0, POISSON_MAX_MEAN_MILLI] . type( error_t ), intent(inout), optional :: err Set to ERROR_VALIDATION when mean_milli is out of range. Return Value integer(kind=int32)","tags":"","url":"interface/next_poisson_int.html"},{"title":"next_range – PIC","text":"public interface next_range Draw a uniform integer in the inclusive range [lo, hi] . The span is computed in unsigned 64-bit arithmetic, so the full range\nof default_int works: next_range(gen, -huge(1)-1, huge(1)) spans\nevery int32 value and is still exactly uniform. Rejection sampling\ngives every value in range exactly one preimage per draw, so there is\nno modulo bias. hi < lo is a usage error: it returns lo and, if err is present,\nsets ERROR_VALIDATION . lo == hi returns lo without consuming a\ndraw. Calls interface~~next_range~~CallsGraph interface~next_range next_range proc~pcg32_next_range pcg32_next_range interface~next_range->proc~pcg32_next_range proc~splitmix64_next_range splitmix64_next_range interface~next_range->proc~splitmix64_next_range proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~pcg32_next_range->proc~error_set proc~pcg32_uniform_below pcg32_uniform_below proc~pcg32_next_range->proc~pcg32_uniform_below proc~u64_add u64_add proc~pcg32_next_range->proc~u64_add proc~splitmix64_next_range->proc~error_set proc~splitmix64_uniform_below splitmix64_uniform_below proc~splitmix64_next_range->proc~splitmix64_uniform_below proc~splitmix64_next_range->proc~u64_add proc~pcg32_next_u64 pcg32_t%pcg32_next_u64 proc~pcg32_uniform_below->proc~pcg32_next_u64 proc~rejection_mask~2 rejection_mask proc~pcg32_uniform_below->proc~rejection_mask~2 proc~u64_less u64_less proc~pcg32_uniform_below->proc~u64_less proc~splitmix64_uniform_below->proc~rejection_mask~2 proc~splitmix64_next_u64 splitmix64_t%splitmix64_next_u64 proc~splitmix64_uniform_below->proc~splitmix64_next_u64 proc~splitmix64_uniform_below->proc~u64_less proc~pcg32_step pcg32_step proc~pcg32_next_u64->proc~pcg32_step proc~u64_