ashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~parse_real_sp_char~~CalledByGraph proc~parse_real_sp_char parse_real_sp_char interface~parse_real parse_real interface~parse_real->proc~parse_real_sp_char proc~parse_real_sp_string parse_real_sp_string interface~parse_real->proc~parse_real_sp_string proc~parse_real_sp_string->proc~parse_real_sp_char proc~cli_get_real_dp cli_t%cli_get_real_dp proc~cli_get_real_dp->interface~parse_real proc~cli_get_real_sp cli_t%cli_get_real_sp proc~cli_get_real_sp->interface~parse_real Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=dp), private :: wide Source Code subroutine parse_real_sp_char ( str , value , err ) !! Parse a character string into a single precision real. !! !! The conversion is done in double precision and then range checked, so !! a value that is finite in `dp` but too large for `sp` is reported as !! an error instead of becoming infinity. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: str real ( sp ), intent ( out ) :: value type ( error_t ), intent ( out ) :: err real ( dp ) :: wide value = 0.0_sp call parse_real_wide ( str , wide , err ) if ( err % has_error ()) return if ( abs ( wide ) > real ( huge ( value ), dp )) then call err % set ( ERROR_PARSE , \"real out of range for single precision: '\" // strip ( str ) // \"'\" ) return end if value = real ( wide , sp ) end subroutine parse_real_sp_char","tags":"","url":"proc/parse_real_sp_char.html"},{"title":"parse_real_sp_string – PIC","text":"private  subroutine parse_real_sp_string(str, value, err) Parse a string_type into a single precision real. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( string_type ), intent(in) :: str real(kind=sp), intent(out) :: value type( error_t ), intent(out) :: err Calls proc~~parse_real_sp_string~~CallsGraph proc~parse_real_sp_string parse_real_sp_string proc~parse_real_sp_char parse_real_sp_char proc~parse_real_sp_string->proc~parse_real_sp_char interface~strip strip proc~parse_real_sp_char->interface~strip proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~parse_real_sp_char->proc~error_has_error proc~error_set error_t%error_set proc~parse_real_sp_char->proc~error_set proc~parse_real_wide parse_real_wide proc~parse_real_sp_char->proc~parse_real_wide proc~strip_char strip_char interface~strip->proc~strip_char proc~strip_string strip_string interface~strip->proc~strip_string proc~parse_real_wide->interface~strip proc~parse_real_wide->proc~error_has_error proc~parse_real_wide->proc~error_set proc~check_exponent check_exponent proc~parse_real_wide->proc~check_exponent proc~skip_sign skip_sign proc~parse_real_wide->proc~skip_sign proc~check_exponent->proc~error_set proc~check_exponent->proc~skip_sign proc~strip_string->interface~strip Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity 