->proc~fail~2 proc~csr_matvec->proc~csr_is_valid proc~csr_row_slice csr_t%csr_row_slice proc~csr_row_slice->proc~fail~2 proc~csr_row_slice->proc~csr_is_valid proc~check_graph check_graph proc~check_graph->proc~csr_is_valid proc~csr_transpose csr_t%csr_transpose proc~csr_transpose->proc~csr_is_valid proc~a_star a_star proc~a_star->proc~check_graph proc~bfs bfs proc~bfs->proc~check_graph proc~connected_components connected_components proc~connected_components->proc~check_graph proc~dijkstra dijkstra proc~dijkstra->proc~check_graph proc~path_cost path_cost proc~path_cost->proc~check_graph Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure subroutine fail ( err , message ) !! Set `err` to `ERROR_VALIDATION` with `message`, when `err` is present. type ( error_t ), intent ( out ), optional :: err character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: message !! Human-readable description of the violation if ( present ( err )) call err % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , message ) end subroutine fail","tags":"","url":"proc/fail~2.html"},{"title":"sort_row – PIC","text":"private pure subroutine sort_row(cols, vals, lo, hi) Insertion-sort one row segment lo:hi by column index. Insertion sort is deliberate: CSR rows are short in practice, the\nsegment is already contiguous, and a stable in-place sort keeps\nequal-column duplicates in their original relative order so the\nsubsequent summation is a plain left-to-right sweep. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(inout) :: cols (:) real(kind=dp), intent(inout) :: vals (:) integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: lo integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: hi Called by proc~~sort_row~~CalledByGraph proc~sort_row sort_row proc~csr_build_from_coo csr_t%csr_build_from_coo proc~csr_build_from_coo->proc~sort_row Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: i integer(kind=default_int), private :: j integer(kind=default_int), private :: key_col real(kind=dp), private :: key_val Source Code pure subroutine sort_row ( cols , vals , lo , hi ) !! Insertion-sort one row segment `lo:hi` by column index. !! !! Insertion sort is deliberate: CSR rows are short in practice, the !! segment is already contiguous, and a stable in-place sort keeps !! equal-column duplicates in their original relative order so the !! subsequent summation is a plain left-to-right sweep. integer ( default_int ), intent ( inout ) :: cols (:) real ( dp ), intent ( inout ) :: vals (:) integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: lo integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: hi integer ( default_int ) :: i , j , key_col real ( dp ) :: key_val do i = lo + 1 , hi key_col = cols ( i ) key_val = vals ( i ) j = i - 1 do while ( j >= lo ) if ( cols ( j ) <= key_col ) exit cols ( j + 1 ) = cols ( j ) vals ( j + 1 ) = vals ( j ) j = j - 1 end do cols ( j + 1 ) = key_col vals ( j + 1 ) = key_val end do end subroutine sort_row","tags":"","url":"proc/sort_row.html"},{"title":"any_of_kind – PIC","text":"private pure function any_of_kind(this, kind) result(r) Whether any declared entry has this kind. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: kind Return Value logical Called by proc~~any_of_kind~~CalledByGraph proc~any_of_kind any_of_kind proc~cli_help_text cli_t%cli_help_text proc~cli_help_text->proc~any_of_kind Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: i Source Code pure function any_of_kind ( this , kind ) result ( r ) !! Whether any declared entry has this kind. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: kind logical :: r integer ( default_int ) :: i r = . false . do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( this % entries ( i )% kind == kind ) then r = . true . return end if end do end function any_of_kind","tags":"","url":"proc/any_of_kind.html"},{"title":"cli_find – PIC","text":"private pure function cli_find(