ocedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: i Source Code pure function cli_find ( this , name ) result ( idx ) !! Index of the entry with this long name, or 0. !! !! A linear walk over the registration array. A command line has tens of !! options, not thousands, and at that size a scan beats hashing while !! needing no map to allocate, copy or free. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Long name to look for, without dashes. integer ( default_int ) :: idx integer ( default_int ) :: i idx = 0_default_int do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( char ( this % entries ( i )% name ) == name ) then idx = i return end if end do end function cli_find","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_find.html"},{"title":"cli_find_short – PIC","text":"private pure function cli_find_short(this, short) result(idx) Index of the entry with this short name, or 0. Empty never matches. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: short Return Value integer(kind=default_int) Called by proc~~cli_find_short~~CalledByGraph proc~cli_find_short cli_find_short proc~cli_parse_args cli_t%cli_parse_args proc~cli_parse_args->proc~cli_find_short proc~cli_parse cli_t%cli_parse proc~cli_parse->proc~cli_parse_args Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: i Source Code pure function cli_find_short ( this , short ) result ( idx ) !! Index of the entry with this short name, or 0. Empty never matches. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: short integer ( default_int ) :: idx integer ( default_int ) :: i idx = 0_default_int if ( len ( short ) == 0 ) return do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( len ( char ( this % entries ( i )% short )) == 0 ) cycle if ( char ( this % entries ( i )% short ) == short ) then idx = i return end if end do end function cli_find_short","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_find_short.html"},{"title":"cli_has – PIC","text":"private pure function cli_has(this, name) result(r) Whether name was declared at all. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name to look for. Return Value logical Calls proc~~cli_has~~CallsGraph proc~cli_has cli_t%cli_has proc~cli_find cli_t%cli_find proc~cli_has->proc~cli_find Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function cli_has ( this , name ) result ( r ) !! Whether `name` was declared at all. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Long name to look for. logical :: r r = this % find ( name ) > 0_default_int end function cli_has","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_has.html"},{"title":"cli_help_requested – PIC","text":"private pure function cli_help_requested(this) result(r) Whether -h or --help was given. The caller decides what to do about it. See “The library never\nprints”. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value logical Source Code pure function cli_help_requested ( this ) result ( r ) !! Whether `-h` or `--help` was given. !! !! The caller decides what to do about it. See \"The library never !! prints\". class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this logical :: r r = this % wants_help end function cli_help_requested","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_help_requested.html"},{"title":"cli_help_text – PIC","text":"private  function cli_help_text(this) result(text) The help text, as a string. Nothing is printed; see the module note. Entries appear in registration order, so the text is stable across\nruns and across compilers. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Calls proc~~cli_help_text~~CallsGraph proc~cli_help_text cli_t%cli_help_text proc~any_of_kind any_of_kind proc~cli_help_text->proc~any_of_kind proc~entry_label entry_label proc~cli_help_text->proc~entry_label Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: i character(len=:), private, allocatable :: label integer(kind=default_int), private :: this_width integer(kind=default_int), private :: width Source Code function cli_help_text ( this ) result ( text ) !! The help text, as a string. Nothing is printed; see the module note. !! !! Entries appear in registration order, so the text is stable across !! runs and across compilers. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this character ( len = :), allocatable :: text integer ( default_int ) :: i , width , this_width character ( len = :), allocatable :: label text = \"Usage: \" // char ( this % program_name ) do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( this % entries ( i )% kind /= KIND_OPTION . and . & this % entries ( i )% kind /= KIND_FLAG ) cycle text = text // \" [options]\" exit end do do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( this % entries ( i )% kind /= KIND_POSITIONAL ) cycle if ( this % entries ( i )% required ) then text = text // \" <\" // char ( this % entries ( i )% name ) // \">\" else text = text // \" [\" // char ( this % entries ( i )% name ) // \"]\" end if end do text = text // new_line ( \"a\" ) if ( len ( char ( this % summary )) > 0 ) then text = text // new_line ( \"a\" ) // char ( this % summary ) // new_line ( \"a\" ) end if ! One pass to find the column, one to write it, so the descriptions line ! up whatever the names are. width = 0_default_int do i = 1_default_int , this % count this_width = len ( entry_label ( this % entries ( i )), kind = default_int ) width = max ( width , this_width ) end do if ( any_of_kind ( this , KIND_POSITIONAL )) then text = text // new_line ( \"a\" ) // \"Arguments:\" // new_line ( \"a\" ) do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( this % entries ( i )% kind /= KIND_POSITIONAL ) cycle label = entry_label ( this % entries ( i )) text = text // \"  \" // label // repeat ( \" \" , width - len ( label )) // & \"  \" // char ( this % entries ( i )% help ) // new_line ( \"a\" ) end do end if text = text // new_line ( \"a\" ) // \"Options:\" // new_line ( \"a\" ) do i = 1_default_int , this % count if ( this % entries ( i )% kind == KIND_POSITIONAL ) cycle label = entry_label ( this % entries ( i )) text = text // \"  \" // label // repeat ( \" \" , width - len ( label )) // & \"  \" // char ( this % entries ( i )% help ) // new_line ( \"a\" ) end do text = text // \"  \" // \"-h, --help\" // repeat ( \" \" , max ( 0_default_int , width - 10_default_int )) // & \"  Show this help\" // new_line ( \"a\" ) end function cli_help_text","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_help_text.html"},{"title":"cli_is_set – PIC","text":"private pure function cli_is_set(this, name) result(r) Whether name appeared on the command line. False for an undeclared name, and false for a declared one that fell\nback to its default. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name to look for. Return Value logical Calls proc~~cli_is_set~~CallsGraph proc~cli_is_set cli_t%cli_is_set proc~cli_find cli_t%cli_find proc~cli_is_set->proc~cli_find Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: idx Source Code pure function cli_is_set ( this , name ) result ( r ) !! Whether `name` appeared on the command line. !! !! False for an undeclared name, and false for a declared one that fell !! back to its default. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Long name to look for. logical :: r integer ( default_int ) :: idx idx = this % find ( name ) r = idx > 0_default_int if ( r ) r = this % entries ( idx )% seen > 0_default_int end function cli_is_set","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_is_set.html"},{"title":"cli_occurrences – PIC","text":"private pure function cli_occurrences(this, name) result(n) How many times name appeared on the command line. get returns the last occurrence. This is how a program that wants\nto reject or warn about a repeat can find out about one. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name to look for. Return Value integer(kind=default_int) Calls proc~~cli_occurrences~~CallsGraph proc~cli_occurrences cli_t%cli_occurrences proc~cli_find cli_t%cli_find proc~cli_occurrences->proc~cli_find Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: idx Source Code pure function cli_occurrences ( this , name ) result ( n ) !! How many times `name` appeared on the command line. !! !! `get` returns the last occurrence. This is how a program that wants !! to reject or warn about a repeat can find out about one. class ( cli_t ), intent ( in ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Long name to look for. integer ( default_int ) :: n integer ( default_int ) :: idx n = 0_default_int idx = this % find ( name ) if ( idx > 0_default_int ) n = this % entries ( idx )% seen end function cli_occurrences","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_occurrences.html"},{"title":"entry_label – PIC","text":"private pure function entry_label(entry) result(label) The left-hand column of one help line. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( entry_t ), intent(in) :: entry Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~entry_label~~CalledByGraph proc~entry_label entry_label proc~cli_help_text cli_t%cli_help_text proc~cli_help_text->proc~entry_label Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function entry_label ( entry ) result ( label ) !! The left-hand column of one help line. type ( entry_t ), intent ( in ) :: entry character ( len = :), allocatable :: label if ( entry % kind == KIND_POSITIONAL ) then label = char ( entry % name ) else if ( len ( char ( entry % short )) > 0 ) then label = \"-\" // char ( entry % short ) // \", --\" // char ( entry % name ) else label = \"    --\" // char ( entry % name ) end if end function entry_label","tags":"","url":"proc/entry_label.html"},{"title":"is_long – PIC","text":"private pure function is_long(arg) result(r) Whether arg is a --name form. A bare -- is not. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: arg Return Value logical Called by proc~~is_long~~CalledByGraph proc~is_long is_long proc~cli_parse_args cli_t%cli_parse_args proc~cli_parse_args->proc~is_long proc~cli_parse cli_t%cli_parse proc~cli_parse->proc~cli_parse_args Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function is_long ( arg ) result ( r ) !! Whether `arg` is a `--name` form. A bare `--` is not. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: arg logical :: r r = . false . if ( len ( arg ) <= 2 ) return r = arg ( 1 : 2 ) == \"--\" end function is_long","tags":"","url":"proc/is_long.html"},{"title":"is_short – PIC","text":"private pure function is_short(arg) result(r) Whether arg is a -s form. A bare - is not, and neither is a\nnegative number, which must be able to reach a positional. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: arg Return Value logical Called by proc~~is_short~~CalledByGraph proc~is_short is_short proc~cli_parse_args cli_t%cli_parse_args proc~cli_parse_args->proc~is_short proc~cli_parse cli_t%cli_parse proc~cli_parse->proc~cli_parse_args Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code pure function is_short ( arg ) result ( r ) !! Whether `arg` is a `-s` form. A bare `-` is not, and neither is a !! negative number, which must be able to reach a positional. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: arg logical :: r r = . false . if ( len ( arg ) /= 2 ) return if ( arg ( 1 : 1 ) /= \"-\" ) return r = . not . ( arg ( 2 : 2 ) >= \"0\" . and . arg ( 2 : 2 ) <= \"9\" ) end function is_short","tags":"","url":"proc/is_short.html"},{"title":"looks_numeric – PIC","text":"private pure function looks_numeric(arg) result(r) Whether arg is a negative number rather than an option. Only the shape is tested, not whether it parses: -5 , -1.5 and -.5 are numbers, -s and -verbose are not. Getting this wrong in\nthe permissive direction would let a mistyped option through as a\npositional, which is the bug this guards. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: arg Token to classify; known to start with - and be longer than one. Return Value logical Called by proc~~looks_numeric~~CalledByGraph proc~looks_numeric looks_numeric proc~cli_parse_args cli_t%cli_parse_args proc~cli_parse_args->proc~looks_numeric proc~cli_parse cli_t%cli_parse proc~cli_parse->proc~cli_parse_args Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=1), private :: c Source Code pure function looks_numeric ( arg ) result ( r ) !! Whether `arg` is a negative number rather than an option. !! !! Only the shape is tested, not whether it parses: `-5`, `-1.5` and !! `-.5` are numbers, `-s` and `-verbose` are not. Getting this wrong in !! the permissive direction would let a mistyped option through as a !! positional, which is the bug this guards. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: arg !! Token to classify; known to start with `-` and be longer than one. logical :: r character ( len = 1 ) :: c r = . false . c = arg ( 2 : 2 ) if ( c >= \"0\" . and . c <= \"9\" ) then r = . true . else if ( c == \".\" . and . len ( arg ) > 2 ) then c = arg ( 3 : 3 ) r = c >= \"0\" . and . c <= \"9\" end if end function looks_numeric","tags":"","url":"proc/looks_numeric.html"},{"title":"cli_add_flag – PIC","text":"private  subroutine cli_add_flag(this, name, help, short) Declare a flag, which takes no value. An absent flag reads back as \"false\" , a present one as \"true\" , so get into a logical works without a special case. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(inout) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name, given on the command line as --name . character(len=*), intent(in) :: help One-line description. character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: short Single-character short name. Calls proc~~cli_add_flag~~CallsGraph proc~cli_add_flag cli_t%cli_add_flag proc~cli_reserve cli_t%cli_reserve proc~cli_add_flag->proc~cli_reserve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine cli_add_flag ( this , name , help , short ) !! Declare a flag, which takes no value. !! !! An absent flag reads back as `\"false\"`, a present one as `\"true\"`, so !! `get` into a `logical` works without a special case. class ( cli_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Long name, given on the command line as `--name`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: help !! One-line description. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: short !! Single-character short name. call this % reserve () this % count = this % count + 1_default_int this % entries ( this % count )% name = name this % entries ( this % count )% help = help this % entries ( this % count )% kind = KIND_FLAG this % entries ( this % count )% required = . false . this % entries ( this % count )% seen = 0_default_int this % entries ( this % count )% value = \"false\" this % entries ( this % count )% default = \"false\" if ( present ( short )) then this % entries ( this % count )% short = short else this % entries ( this % count )% short = \"\" end if end subroutine cli_add_flag","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_add_flag.html"},{"title":"cli_add_option – PIC","text":"private  subroutine cli_add_option(this, name, help, short, default) Declare an option that takes a value. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(inout) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name, given on the command line as --name . character(len=*), intent(in) :: help One-line description. character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: short Single-character short name, given as -s . character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: default Value get returns when the option is absent; empty if omitted. Calls proc~~cli_add_option~~CallsGraph proc~cli_add_option cli_t%cli_add_option proc~cli_reserve cli_t%cli_reserve proc~cli_add_option->proc~cli_reserve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine cli_add_option ( this , name , help , short , default ) !! Declare an option that takes a value. class ( cli_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Long name, given on the command line as `--name`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: help !! One-line description. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: short !! Single-character short name, given as `-s`. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: default !! Value `get` returns when the option is absent; empty if omitted. call this % reserve () this % count = this % count + 1_default_int this % entries ( this % count )% name = name this % entries ( this % count )% help = help this % entries ( this % count )% kind = KIND_OPTION this % entries ( this % count )% required = . false . this % entries ( this % count )% seen = 0_default_int if ( present ( short )) then this % entries ( this % count )% short = short else this % entries ( this % count )% short = \"\" end if if ( present ( default )) then this % entries ( this % count )% value = default this % entries ( this % count )% default = default else this % entries ( this % count )% value = \"\" this % entries ( this % count )% default = \"\" end if end subroutine cli_add_option","tags":"","url":"proc/cli_add_option.html"},{"title":"cli_add_positional – PIC","text":"private  subroutine cli_add_positional(this, name, help, required, default) Declare a positional argument, filled in registration order. Type Bound cli_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(inout) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Name used to read the value back, and in the usage line. character(len=*), intent(in) :: help One-line description. logical, intent(in), optional :: required Whether a parse without it is ERROR_VALIDATION ; default false. character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: default Value get returns when the argument is absent. Calls proc~~cli_add_positional~~CallsGraph proc~cli_add_positional cli_t%cli_add_positional proc~cli_reserve cli_t%cli_reserve proc~cli_add_positional->proc~cli_reserve Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine cli_add_positional ( this , name , help , required , default ) !! Declare a positional argument, filled in registration order. class ( cli_t ), intent ( inout ) :: this character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: name !! Name used to read the value back, and in the usage line. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: help !! One-line description. logical , intent ( in ), optional :: required !! Whether a parse without it is `ERROR_VALIDATION`; default false. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ), optional :: default !! Value `get` returns when the argument is absent. call this % reserve () this % count = this % count + 1_default_int this % entries ( this % count )% name = name this % entries ( this % count )% help = help this % entries ( this % count )% short = \"\" this % entries ( this % count )% kind = KIND_POSITIONAL this % entries ( this % count )% seen = 0_default_int if ( present ( required )) then this % entries ( this % count )% required = required else this % entries ( this % count )% required = . false . end if if ( present ( default )) then this % entries ( this % count )% value = default this % entries ( this % count )% default = default else this % entries ( this % count )% value = \"\" this % entries ( this % count )% default 