ded, point_pos, dec) result(string) Place the decimal point in an already rounded digit string. The invariant maintained by round_decimal is that n_rounded equals point_pos + dec whenever any digit survives, so splitting at point_pos always leaves exactly dec fractional digits. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name logical, intent(in) :: negative character(len=*), intent(in) :: rounded integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n_rounded integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: point_pos integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: dec Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Called by proc~~assemble_fixed~~CalledByGraph proc~assemble_fixed assemble_fixed proc~to_string_fixed_dp to_string_fixed_dp proc~to_string_fixed_dp->proc~assemble_fixed interface~to_string_fixed to_string_fixed interface~to_string_fixed->proc~to_string_fixed_dp proc~to_string_fixed_sp to_string_fixed_sp interface~to_string_fixed->proc~to_string_fixed_sp proc~to_string_fixed_sp->proc~to_string_fixed_dp Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=:), private, allocatable :: frac_part character(len=:), private, allocatable :: int_part Source Code pure function assemble_fixed ( negative , rounded , n_rounded , point_pos , dec ) result ( string ) !! Place the decimal point in an already rounded digit str