ine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=LIMB_DIGITS), private :: chunk integer(kind=default_int), private :: first integer(kind=default_int), private :: i integer(kind=default_int), private :: pos Source Code pure subroutine bd_to_digits ( limb , n_limb , exact , n_exact ) !! Write the big integer out as a decimal digit string, no leading zeros. integer ( int64 ), intent ( in ) :: limb (:) integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: n_limb character ( len =* ), intent ( out ) :: exact integer ( default_int ), intent ( out ) :: n_exact character ( len = LIMB_DIGITS ) :: chunk integer ( default_int ) :: i , first , pos exact = \"\" call limb_to_digits ( limb ( n_limb ), chunk ) first = 1_default_int do while ( first < LIMB_DIGITS . and . chunk ( first : first ) == \"0\" ) first = first + 1_default_int end do pos = LIMB_DIGITS - first + 1_default_int exact ( 1 : pos ) = chunk ( first : LIMB_DIGITS ) do i = n_limb - 1_default_int , 1_default_int , - 1_default_int call limb_to_digits ( limb ( i ), chunk ) exact ( pos + 1_default_int : pos + LIMB_DIGITS ) = chunk pos = pos + LIMB_DIGITS end do n_exact = pos end subroutine bd_to_digits","tags":"","url":"proc/bd_to_digits.html"},{"title":"expand_exact – PIC","text":"private pure subroutine expand_exact(value, exact, n_exact, point_pos) Exact decimal expansion of a finite, strictly positive value. An IEEE value is mantissa * 2**pow2 with an integer mantissa. When pow2 is negative that equals mantissa * 5**(-pow2) / 10**(-pow2) ,\nso the exact decimal digits are the digits of the big integer mantissa * 5**(-pow2) with the point shifted -pow2 places. When pow2 is positive the value is the integer mantissa * 2**pow2 .\nEither way no rounding whatsoever happens here. On return the value equals 0.<digits> * 10**point_pos , where <digits> is exact(1:n_exact) . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: value character(len=*), intent(out) :: exact integer(kind=default_int), intent(out) :: n_exact integer(kind=default_int), intent(out) :: point_pos Calls proc~~expand_exact~~CallsGraph proc~expand_exact expand_exact proc~bd_mul_pow bd_mul_pow proc~expand_exact->proc~bd_mul_pow proc~bd_set bd_set proc~expand_exact->proc~bd_set proc~bd_to_digits bd_to_digits proc~expand_exact->proc~bd_to_digits proc~bd_mul_small bd_mul_small proc~bd_mul_pow->proc~bd_mul_small proc~limb_to_digits limb_to_digits proc~bd_to_digits->proc~limb_to_digits Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Interface Interface Type Bound Procedure Type Bound Procedure Unknown Procedure Type Unknown Procedure Type Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a procedure to one which it calls. Dashed \narrows point from an interface to procedures which implement that interface.\nThis could include the module procedures in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Called by proc~~expand_exact~~CalledByGraph proc~expand_exact expand_exact proc~to_string_fixed_dp to_string_fixed_dp proc~to_string_fixed_dp->proc~expand_exact proc~to_string_sci_dp to_string_sci_dp proc~to_string_sci_dp->proc~expand_exact interface~to_st