in a generic interface or the\nimplementation in a submodule of an interface in a parent module. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Source Code subroutine soa_write_prologue ( unit , schema , n , err ) !! Write the stream header, the schema record and the element count. !! !! Call this once on a freshly opened stream unit, before any field !! record. integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: unit !! Stream unit opened for unformatted stream writing. character ( len =* ), intent ( in ) :: schema !! The container's schema string. integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: n !! Number of live elements about to be written. type ( error_t ), intent ( inout ) :: err !! Error state. if ( n < 0 ) then call err % set ( ERROR_VALIDATION , \"soa: cannot serialize a negative element count \" // & to_char ( int ( n , int64 ))) return end if call write_header ( unit , err ) if ( err % has_error ()) return call write_array ( unit , schema , err ) if ( err % has_error ()) return call write_array ( unit , [ int ( n , int64 )], err ) end subroutine soa_write_prologue","tags":"","url":"proc/soa_write_prologue.html"},{"title":"soa_hash64_int32_field – PIC","text":"private  subroutine soa_hash64_int32_field(hasher, values, n) Fold the first n elements of an integer(int32) field into a 64-bit hash. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( array_hash64_t ), intent(inout) :: hasher integer(kind=int32), intent(in), allocatable :: values (:) integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n Calls proc~~soa_hash64_int32_field~~CallsGraph proc~soa_hash64_int32_field soa_hash64_int32_field none~update~2 array_hash64_t%update proc~soa_hash64_int32_field->none~update~2 proc~update64_cdp_0 array_hash64_t%update64_cdp_0 none~update~2->proc~update64_cdp_0 proc~update64_cdp_1 array_hash64_t%update64_cdp_1 none~update~2->proc~update64_cdp_1 proc~update64_cdp_2 array_hash64_t%update64_cdp_2 none~update~2->proc~upd