e , intent ( in ) :: values (:) integer ( default_int ), intent ( in ) :: n if (. not . allocated ( values )) return if ( n <= 0 ) return call hasher % update ( values ( 1 : n )) end subroutine soa_hash64_real_sp_field","tags":"","url":"proc/soa_hash64_real_sp_field.html"},{"title":"soa_hash_begin_32 – PIC","text":"private  subroutine soa_hash_begin_32(hasher, schema, n) Reset a 32-bit hash accumulator and fold in a container’s identity. Feeds the schema string and then the element count as an explicit int64 , so the digest is the same in a default build and in a PIC_DEFAULT_INT8 build. Folding the schema first means two\ncontainers with different field lists cannot produce the same digest\neven when their numeric payloads agree, and folding the count means an\nempty container is distinguishable from an absent one. The caller then folds in every field’s live slice, in declaration\norder, and takes hasher%digest() . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( array_hash_t ), intent(inout) :: hasher Accumulator to restart. character(len=*), intent(in) :: schema The container’s schema string. integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n Number of live elements. Calls proc~~soa_hash_begin_32~~CallsGraph proc~soa_hash_begin_32 soa_hash_begin_32 none~update array_hash_t%update proc~soa_hash_begin_32->none~update proc~array_hash_reset array_hash_t%array_hash_reset proc~soa_hash_begin_32->proc~array_hash_reset proc~update_cdp_0 array_hash_t%update_cdp_0 none~update->proc~update_cdp_0 proc~update_cdp_1 array_hash_t%update_cdp_1 none~update->proc~update_cdp_1 proc~update_cdp_2 array_hash_t%update_cdp_2 none~update->proc~update_cdp_2 proc~update_cdp_3 array_hash_t%update_cdp_3 none~update->proc~update_cdp_3 proc~update_char_0 array_hash_t%update_char_0 none~update->proc~update_char_0 proc~update_char_1 array_hash_t%update_char_1 none~update->proc~update_char_1 proc~update_csp_0 array_hash_t%update_csp_0 none~update->proc~update_csp_0 proc~update_csp_1 array_hash_t%updat