 () return end if call soa_read_field ( unit , \"mass\" , this % mass , n , swapped , err ) if ( err % has_error ()) then call this % deallocate () return end if call soa_read_field ( unit , \"active\" , this % active , n , swapped , err ) if ( err % has_error ()) then call this % deallocate () return end if this % extent % used = n this % extent % capacity = n end subroutine particle_soa_deserialize","tags":"","url":"proc/particle_soa_deserialize.html"},{"title":"particle_soa_resize – PIC","text":"private  subroutine particle_soa_resize(this, n, err) Change the number of live elements, preserving the elements that\nsurvive. min(size(), n) leading elements of every field keep their values.\nGrowing sets the newly exposed elements to the zero value of their\ntype; shrinking only lowers the live count. Capacity grows\ngeometrically and never shrinks – see pic_soa . On failure the container is left exactly as it was. Type Bound particle_soa_t Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( particle_soa_t ), intent(inout) :: this Container to resize. integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n New number of live elements. Must not be negative. type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err Error state, ERROR_VALIDATION on a negative n and ERROR_ALLOC if a field array cannot be allocated. Calls proc~~particle_soa_resize~~CallsGraph proc~particle_soa_resize particle_soa_t%particle_soa_resize interface~soa_resize_field soa_resize_field proc~particle_soa_resize->interface~soa_resize_field proc~error_has_error error_t%error_has_error proc~particle_soa_resize->proc~error_has_error proc~soa_plan_resize soa_plan_resize proc~particle_soa_resize->proc~soa_plan_resize proc~soa_resize_int32_field soa_resize_int32_field interface~soa_resize_field->proc~soa_resize_int32_field proc~soa_resize_int64_field soa_resize_int64_field interface~soa_resize_field->proc~soa_resize_int64_field proc~soa_resize_logical_field soa_resize_logical_field interface~soa_resize_field->proc~soa_resize_logical_f