ersion <= PIC_FORMAT_VERSION and reject anything else with ERROR_VALIDATION . integer(kind=int64), public, parameter :: PIC_HEADER_BYTES = 16_int64 Size of the stream header in bytes. character(len=*), public, parameter :: PIC_MAGIC = \"PIC1\" Four byte ASCII magic written at offset 0 of every stream. Being\ncharacters it has no byte order of its own, which is what makes it\nusable to reject a foreign file before anything else is decoded. integer(kind=int64), public, parameter :: PIC_RECORD_HEADER_BYTES = 12_int64 Size of one record header, tag plus element count, in bytes. integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: PIC_TAG_CHAR = 5_int32 Record tag for a character scalar, 1 byte per element. integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: PIC_TAG_INT32 = 1_int32 Record tag for integer(int32) arrays, 4 bytes per element. integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: PIC_TAG_INT64 = 2_int32 Record tag for integer(int64) arrays, 8 bytes per element. integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: PIC_TAG_REAL_DP = 4_int32 Record tag for real(dp) arrays, 8 bytes per element. integer(kind=int32), public, parameter :: PIC_TAG_REAL_SP = 3_int32 Record tag for real(sp) arrays, 4 bytes per element. integer(kind=int32), private, parameter :: BITS_PER_BYTE = 8_int32 Width of one byte field, used by the byte reversal helpers. integer(kind=int32), private, parameter :: PIC_ENDIAN_MARK = 16909060_int32 0x01020304 , spelled in decimal so that no BOZ literal appears in an\ninitializer, since gfortran and ifx disagree about the kind of those.\nWritten natively: a reader that sees the byte reversed value 0x04030201 knows the file came from the opposite byte order. integer(kind=int32), private, parameter :: RESERVED_WORD = 0_int32 Value written into the reserved header slot. Interfaces public        interface read_array Read one record back, validating its type tag and its length. Usage: call read_array(unit, values, swapped, err) values is allocatable and is allocated to the length stored in the\nrecord. swapped is the flag returned by read_header ; when it is\ntrue every multi-byte element is byte reversed after reading. Fails with ERROR_VALIDATION if the record holds a different type\nthan the one requested, and with ERROR_IO if the payload announced\nby the record header runs past the end of the file. private  subroutine read_int32_array (unit, values, swapped, err) Read an integer(int32) array record. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: unit integer(kind=int32), intent(out), allocatable :: values (:) logical, intent(in) :: swapped type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private  subroutine read_int64_array (unit, values, swapped, err) Read an integer(int64) array record. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: unit integer(kind=int64), intent(out), allocatable :: values (:) logical, intent(in) :: swapped type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private  subroutine read_real_sp_array (unit, values, swapped, err) Read a real(sp) array record. On the native path the values are read straight into values . On the\nforeign endian path the same bytes are read into an int32 buffer,\nreversed with integer arithmetic, and only then reinterpreted. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: unit real(kind=sp), intent(out), allocatable :: values (:) logical, intent(in) :: swapped type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private  subroutine read_real_dp_array (unit, values, swapped, err) Read a real(dp) array record. See read_real_sp_array for the way\nthe foreign endian path is kept away from the native one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: unit real(kind=dp), intent(out), allocatable :: values (:) logical, intent(in) :: swapped type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private  subroutine read_char_record (unit, text, swapped, err) Read a character scalar record into a deferred lengt