=> get_flops procedure, public, non_overridable :: reset => reset_flop_counter Functions private  function get_flops (self) result(flops) Get the int64 number of FLOPs we currently have in the counter Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( flop_recorder_type ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=int64) Subroutines private  subroutine add_flops (self, flops) Add an int64 variable which contains the FLOPs\nwe use int64 since we might reach very large FLOP counts Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( flop_recorder_type ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: flops private  subroutine reset_flop_counter (self) Resets the flop counter to 0_int64 Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( flop_recorder_type ), intent(inout) :: self","tags":"","url":"module/pic_flop_recorder.html"},{"title":"pic_csr – PIC","text":"A compressed sparse row matrix: the standard layout for sparse linear\n algebra and, identically, for adjacency lists of weighted graphs. pic_graph builds its shortest-path algorithms directly on this type. ### Layout A csr_t holds the usual triple, all of it one-based: row_ptr(1:nrow+1) - row_ptr(i) is the index in col_idx / values of the first stored entry of row i , and row_ptr(i+1) - 1 the index\n   of its last. row_ptr(1) is always 1 and row_ptr(nrow+1) is nnz + 1 . col_idx(1:nnz) - column index of each stored entry, sorted\n   ascending within every row. values(1:nnz) - the matching real(dp) values. An empty row i is represented by row_ptr(i) == row_ptr(i+1) , which\n makes every row loop do k = row_ptr(i), row_ptr(i+1) - 1 iterate zero\n times. That case is explicitly supported and tested. ### Duplicate coordinate entries are summed build_from_coo accepts coordinate triplets in any order. Repeated (i, j) coordinates are summed , which is the conventional\n finite-element assembly semantics and makes the builder usable directly\n as an assembly routine. Duplicates are not an error. ### Components are public on purpose The three arrays and the shape are public components so that consumers\n such as pic_graph can walk rows without copying. Writing to them by\n hand can produce a structurally broken matrix, which is exactly what is_valid exists to detect; matvec , transpose and row_slice call\n it before touching any index, so a malformed matrix produces an error_t rather than an out-of-bounds access. ### Usage type ( csr_t ) :: a type ( error_t ) :: err real ( dp ) :: y ( 2 ) call a % build_from_coo ( 2_default_int , 2_default_int , & [ 1_default_int , 2_default_int ], & [ 2_default_int , 1_default_int ], & [ 3.0_dp , 4.0_dp ], err ) call a % matvec ([ 1.0_dp , 1.0_dp ], y , err ) Uses pic_types pic_error module~~pic_csr~~UsesGraph module~pic_csr pic_csr module~pic_error pic_error module~pic_csr->module~pic_error module~pic_types pic_types module~pic_csr->module~pic_types module~pic_error->module~pic_types module~pic_global_definitions pic_global_definitions module~pic_error->module~pic_global_definitions iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~pic_types->iso_c_binding iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~pic_types->iso_fortran_env module~pic_global_definitions->module~pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~pic_csr~~UsedByGraph module~pic_csr pic_csr module~pic_graph pic_graph module~pic_graph->module~pic_csr Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Derived Types type, public :: csr_t Compressed sparse row matrix with real(dp) values. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), public, allocatable :: col_idx (:) Column index of every stored entry, ascending within each row integer(kind=default_int), public :: ncol = 0 Number of columns; prefer the n_cols accessor when reading integer(kind=default_int), public :: nrow = 0 Number of rows; prefer the n_rows accessor when reading integer(kind=default_int), public, allocatable :: row_ptr (:) Row start offsets, size nrow + 1 , one-based real(kind=dp), public, allocatable :: values (:) Value of every stored entry, parallel to col_idx Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: build_from_coo => csr_build_from_coo procedure, public :: destroy => csr_destroy procedure, public :: is_valid => csr_is_valid procedure, public :: matvec => csr_matvec procedure, public :: n_cols => csr_n_cols procedure, public :: n_rows => csr_n_rows procedure, public :: nnz => csr_nnz procedure, public :: row_slice => csr_row_slice procedure, public :: transpose => csr_transpose Functions private  function csr_is_valid (self, err) result(ok) Check that the stored triple is structurally consistent. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self type( error_t ), intent(out), optional :: err Return Value logical .true. when the matrix is structurally sound private pure function csr_n_cols (self) result(n) Number of columns of the matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function csr_n_rows (self) result(n) Number of rows of the matrix. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function csr_nnz (self) result(n) Number of stored entries, including any explicitly stored zeros. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) Subroutines private  subroutine csr_build_from_coo (self, n_rows, n_cols, rows, cols, vals, err) Build the matrix from coordinate (COO) triplets. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n_rows Number of rows of the assembled matrix integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n_cols Number of columns of the assembled matrix integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: rows (:) Row coordinate of each triplet integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: cols (:) Column coordinate of each triplet real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: vals (:) Value of each triplet type( error_t ), intent(out), optional :: err private  subroutine csr_destroy (self) Release all storage and reset the matrix to an empty 0 by 0 one. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(inout) :: self private  subroutine csr_matvec (self, x, y, err) Sparse matrix-vector product y = A*x . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: x (:) Input vector of length n_cols real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: y (:) Output vector of length n_rows type( error_t ), intent(out), optional :: err private  subroutine csr_row_slice (self, i, cols, vals, err) Copy out the column indices and values stored in row i . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: i Row to read, in 1:nrow integer(kind=default_int), intent(out), allocatable :: cols (:) Column indices of row i , ascending real(kind=dp), intent(out), allocatable :: vals (:) Values of row i , parallel to cols type( error_t ), intent(out), optional :: err private  subroutine csr_transpose (self, at, err) Build the transpose of this matrix into at . Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( csr_t ), intent(in) :: self type( csr_t ), intent(out) :: at Receives the transpose type( error_t ), intent(out), optional :: err private pure subroutine fail (err, message) Set err to ERROR_VALIDATION with message , when err is present. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( error_t ), intent(out), optional :: err character(len=*), intent(in) :: message Human-readable description of the violation private pure subroutine sort_row (cols, vals, lo, hi) Insertion-sort one row segment lo:hi by column index. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(inout) :: cols (:) real(kind=dp), intent(inout) :: vals (:) integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: lo integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: hi","tags":"","url":"module/pic_csr.html"},{"title":"pic_cli – PIC","text":"A declarative command line parser. Declare what the program accepts, parse once, then read values back by\nname. Nothing is printed and nothing is stopped: every failure comes\nback as an error_t , and even --help is reported rather than acted\non, because a library has no business deciding that a process should\nend or where its text should go. See “The library never prints” below. Quick start type ( cli_t ) :: cli type ( error_t ) :: err integer ( int64 ) :: seed call cli % set_program ( \"fairport\" , \"Deterministic airport simulator\" ) call cli % add_positional ( \"scenario\" , \"Scenario script to run\" , required = . true .) call cli % add_option ( \"seed\" , \"Master RNG seed\" , short = \"s\" , default = \"0\" ) call cli % add_flag ( \"hash\" , \"Print the event-log hash and exit\" ) call cli % parse ( err ) if (. haserror . err ) call err % fatal () if ( cli % help_requested ()) then write ( * , \"(a)\" ) cli % help_text () stop 0 end if call cli % get ( \"seed\" , seed , err ) if ( cli % is_set ( \"hash\" )) ... Grammar --name value and --name=value -s value for an option given a short name -- ends option parsing; everything after it is a positional, even if\n  it starts with a dash -h and --help are reserved: they set help_requested() and are\n  never passed through as options A flag takes no value. --flag=value is an error rather than a silently\nignored value. Out of scope in this version: subcommands, grouped short flags ( -abc ),\nenvironment variable fallbacks, and range validation. Repeated options The last occurrence wins, which is what a shell user expects when they\nedit a long command line by appending to it. The earlier values are not\nlost silently, though: occurrences(name) reports how many times an\noption was given, so a program that wants to reject a repeat, or warn\nabout one, can. The library never prints help_text() returns the text. help_requested() reports the request.\nNeither writes to a unit, and nothing here calls stop . A library that\nprints has decided that the program has a terminal, that the text goes\nto output_unit rather than to a log or a socket, and that English is\nwanted. A library that stops has decided that the program has nothing\nleft to clean up. Those are the caller’s decisions. Testing parse_args is the real implementation and takes the arguments as an\narray. parse only collects get_command_argument and forwards to it.\nTests therefore never need a real command line, and every case below –\nincluding the ones that are errors – is exercised without a shell. Uses pic_string_type pic_types pic_tokenizer pic_error module~~pic_cli~~UsesGraph module~pic_cli pic_cli module~pic_error pic_error module~pic_cli->module~pic_error module~pic_string_type pic_string_type module~pic_cli->module~pic_string_type module~pic_tokenizer pic_tokenizer module~pic_cli->module~pic_tokenizer module~pic_types pic_types module~pic_cli->module~pic_types module~pic_error->module~pic_types module~pic_global_definitions pic_global_definitions module~pic_error->module~pic_global_definitions module~pic_string_type->module~pic_types module~pic_ascii pic_ascii module~pic_string_type->module~pic_ascii module~pic_optional_value pic_optional_value module~pic_string_type->module~pic_optional_value module~pic_tokenizer->module~pic_error module~pic_tokenizer->module~pic_string_type module~pic_tokenizer->module~pic_types module~pic_tokenizer->module~pic_ascii module~pic_strings pic_strings module~pic_tokenizer->module~pic_strings iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~pic_types->iso_c_binding iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~pic_types->iso_fortran_env module~pic_ascii->module~pic_types module~pic_global_definitions->module~pic_types module~pic_optional_value->module~pic_types module~pic_strings->module~pic_string_type module~pic_strings->module~pic_types module~pic_strings->iso_c_binding module~pic_strings->module~pic_ascii module~pic_strings->module~pic_optional_value Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private, parameter :: INITIAL_CAPACITY = 8_default_int Entries reserved on the first registration; grown by doubling. integer(kind=default_int), private, parameter :: KIND_FLAG = 2_default_int An entry that takes no value. integer(kind=default_int), private, parameter :: KIND_OPTION = 1_default_int An entry that takes a value. integer(kind=default_int), private, parameter :: KIND_POSITIONAL = 3_default_int An entry filled from the argument order rather than by name. Derived Types type, public :: cli_t A command line interface: what is accepted, and what was given. Read more… Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: count = 0_default_int Entries in use; entries may be longer. type( entry_t ), private, allocatable :: entries (:) Declared entries, in registration order, so help_text is stable. logical, private :: parsed = .false. Set once a parse has completed, successfully or not. type( string_type ), private :: program_name Name used in the usage line. type( string_type ), private :: summary One-line description of the program. logical, private :: wants_help = .false. Set when -h or --help was seen. Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: add_flag => cli_add_flag procedure, public :: add_option => cli_add_option procedure, public :: add_positional => cli_add_positional generic, public :: get => get_string , get_char , get_int32 , get_int64 , get_real_sp , get_real_dp , get_logical procedure, public :: has => cli_has procedure, public :: help_requested => cli_help_requested procedure, public :: help_text => cli_help_text procedure, public :: is_set => cli_is_set procedure, public :: occurrences => cli_occurrences procedure, public :: parse => cli_parse procedure, public :: parse_args => cli_parse_args procedure, public :: set_program => cli_set_program procedure, private :: find => cli_find procedure, private :: get_char => cli_get_char procedure, private :: get_int32 => cli_get_int32 procedure, private :: get_int64 => cli_get_int64 procedure, private :: get_logical => cli_get_logical procedure, private :: get_real_dp => cli_get_real_dp procedure, private :: get_real_sp => cli_get_real_sp procedure, private :: get_string => cli_get_string procedure, private :: reserve => cli_reserve type, private :: entry_t One declared option, flag or positional. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial type( string_type ), private :: default The declared default, kept so that a second parse_args can put value back. Without it a re-parse silently inherits the previous\nrun’s values. type( string_type ), private :: help One-line description, for help_text . integer(kind=default_int), private :: kind = KIND_OPTION One of the KIND_* codes. type( string_type ), private :: name Long name, without the leading dashes. logical, private :: required = .false. Whether a missing positional is an error. integer(kind=default_int), private :: seen = 0_default_int How many times this entry appeared on the command line. type( string_type ), private :: short Single-character short name, or empty if there is none. type( string_type ), private :: value Current value: the default until parsing overwrites it. Functions private pure function any_of_kind (this, kind) result(r) Whether any declared entry has this kind. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: kind Return Value logical private pure function cli_find (this, name) result(idx) Index of the entry with this long name, or 0. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name to look for, without dashes. Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function cli_find_short (this, short) result(idx) Index of the entry with this short name, or 0. Empty never matches. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: short Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function cli_has (this, name) result(r) Whether name was declared at all. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( cli_t ), intent(in) :: this character(len=*), intent(in) :: name Long name to look for. Return Value logical private pure function cli_help