(in) :: array (:) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable private  function to_char_vector_sp (array) result(trimmed_str) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value character(len=:), allocatable Subroutines public  subroutine print_asterisk_row (n) prints a convenient row of asterisks of length n Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: n number of asterisks to print private  subroutine set_precision_internal (precision) Set the precision for real numbers Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: precision","tags":"","url":"module/pic_io.html"},{"title":"pic_fixed_array – PIC","text":"Fixed-capacity (“in place”) array containers. Motivation: HPC inner loops where the upper bound on the number of\nelements is known ahead of time, where an allocate is unacceptable,\nand where push/pop/size semantics with bounds checking are still\nwanted. The element storage is a fixed-size component, never allocatable and never a pointer , so an object of these types can\nlive on the stack, in a block construct, or as a local of an\nOpenMP/OpenACC region without touching the heap. Capacity is the module parameter PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY . It is a\ncompile-time constant shared by every instance; change it in one place\nif your problem needs a different bound. A deliberate design choice is\nthat this module does not use a parameterized derived type (a len type parameter would be the textbook answer) because PDT support is\npoor or absent on several of the compilers PIC exists to support. Usage:\n  type(fixed_array_int_t) :: stack\n  type(error_t) :: err\n  integer(default_int) :: value call stack%push_back(42_default_int, err)\n  if (err%has_error()) call err%fatal()\n  call stack%pop_back(value, err) Every operation that can fail reports through error_t with ERROR_VALIDATION : overflowing the capacity, popping an empty\ncontainer and out-of-range indexing are all errors, never a silent\nwrite past the end and never a crash. The err argument is intent(inout) and is written to only when\nthe operation fails; a successful call leaves it exactly as it was.\nThis is deliberate and is what keeps the promise of no heap traffic: error_t has an allocatable message component, so an intent(out) error argument would make the compiler emit a\ndeallocation of that component on entry to every single call,\nputting a free in the middle of the hot loop. Callers that reuse\none error_t across several calls should call err%clear() between\nthem, exactly as elsewhere in PIC. Uses pic_types pic_error module~~pic_fixed_array~~UsesGraph module~pic_fixed_array pic_fixed_array module~pic_error pic_error module~pic_fixed_array->module~pic_error module~pic_types pic_types module~pic_fixed_array->module~pic_types module~pic_error->module~pic_types module~pic_global_definitions pic_global_definitions module~pic_error->module~pic_global_definitions iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~pic_types->iso_c_binding iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~pic_types->iso_fortran_env module~pic_global_definitions->module~pic_types Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Variables Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), public, parameter :: PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY = 256_default_int Maximum number of elements any fixed array can hold. Compile-time\nconstant: the storage of every instance is exactly this many\nelements, so a fixed_array_dp_t occupies 256 doubles (2 KiB)\nregardless of how many elements are live. character(len=*), private, parameter :: MSG_OUT_OF_RANGE = \"fixed array index out of range, valid range is 1:size()\" character(len=*), private, parameter :: MSG_OVERFLOW = \"fixed array is full, cannot push_back beyond PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY\" character(len=*), private, parameter :: MSG_UNDERFLOW = \"fixed array is empty, cannot pop_back\" Derived Types type, public :: fixed_array_dp_t Bounded array of real(dp) with fixed inline storage. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial real(kind=dp), private :: items (PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY) Inline storage. Deliberately not allocatable : no heap, ever.\nElements above n_items are undefined and must not be read. integer(kind=default_int), private :: n_items = 0 Number of live elements, always in 0:PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: as_array => fixed_array_dp_as_array procedure, public :: at => fixed_array_dp_at procedure, public :: capacity => fixed_array_dp_capacity procedure, public :: clear => fixed_array_dp_clear procedure, public :: get_unchecked => fixed_array_dp_get_unchecked procedure, public :: is_empty => fixed_array_dp_is_empty procedure, public :: is_full => fixed_array_dp_is_full procedure, public :: pop_back => fixed_array_dp_pop_back procedure, public :: push_back => fixed_array_dp_push_back procedure, public :: size => fixed_array_dp_size type, public :: fixed_array_int_t Bounded array of integer(default_int) with fixed inline storage. Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial integer(kind=default_int), private :: items (PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY) Inline storage. Deliberately not allocatable : no heap, ever.\nElements above n_items are undefined and must not be read. integer(kind=default_int), private :: n_items = 0 Number of live elements, always in 0:PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: as_array => fixed_array_int_as_array procedure, public :: at => fixed_array_int_at procedure, public :: capacity => fixed_array_int_capacity procedure, public :: clear => fixed_array_int_clear procedure, public :: get_unchecked => fixed_array_int_get_unchecked procedure, public :: is_empty => fixed_array_int_is_empty procedure, public :: is_full => fixed_array_int_is_full procedure, public :: pop_back => fixed_array_int_pop_back procedure, public :: push_back => fixed_array_int_push_back procedure, public :: size => fixed_array_int_size Functions private pure function fixed_array_dp_as_array (self) result(arr) Copy of the live elements as a plain array of extent size() ,\nnot capacity() . Returns a zero-length array when empty. This is\nhow the contents are handed to ordinary Fortran routines; note\nthat it is the one operation here that does allocate, so keep it\nout of the hot path. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value real(kind=dp), allocatable, (:) private pure function fixed_array_dp_capacity (self) result(n) Maximum number of elements, i.e. PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function fixed_array_dp_get_unchecked (self, index) result(value) UNCHECKED element access for inner loops: no bounds check at all.\nThe caller is responsible for guaranteeing 1 <= index <= size() ,\ntypically by looping over 1, array%size() . Reading an index\noutside that range returns undefined data. Use at unless the\nbounds check is measurably in the way. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: index Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function fixed_array_dp_is_empty (self) result(empty) True when no elements are live. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical private pure function fixed_array_dp_is_full (self) result(full) True when a further push_back would fail. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical private pure function fixed_array_dp_size (self) result(n) Number of live elements. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function fixed_array_int_as_array (self) result(arr) Copy of the live elements as a plain array of extent size() ,\nnot capacity() . Returns a zero-length array when empty. This is\nhow the contents are handed to ordinary Fortran routines; note\nthat it is the one operation here that does allocate, so keep it\nout of the hot path. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int), allocatable, (:) private pure function fixed_array_int_capacity (self) result(n) Maximum number of elements, i.e. PIC_FIXED_ARRAY_CAPACITY . Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function fixed_array_int_get_unchecked (self, index) result(value) UNCHECKED element access for inner loops: no bounds check at all.\nThe caller is responsible for guaranteeing 1 <= index <= size() ,\ntypically by looping over 1, array%size() . Reading an index\noutside that range returns undefined data. Use at unless the\nbounds check is measurably in the way. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: index Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function fixed_array_int_is_empty (self) result(empty) True when no elements are live. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical private pure function fixed_array_int_is_full (self) result(full) True when a further push_back would fail. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value logical private pure function fixed_array_int_size (self) result(n) Number of live elements. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self Return Value integer(kind=default_int) Subroutines private pure subroutine fixed_array_dp_at (self, index, value, err) Bounds-checked element access, 1-based. Any index outside 1:size() (including indices that are within the capacity but\nbeyond the live elements) sets value to zero and err to ERROR_VALIDATION . On success err is left untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(in) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: index real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: value type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private pure subroutine fixed_array_dp_clear (self) Drop every element. The storage itself is untouched, so this is a\nsingle integer assignment; the array can be reused immediately. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(inout) :: self private pure subroutine fixed_array_dp_pop_back (self, value, err) Remove and return the last element (LIFO). On an empty array value is set to zero and err is set to ERROR_VALIDATION .\nOn success err is left untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=dp), intent(out) :: value type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private pure subroutine fixed_array_dp_push_back (self, value, err) Append an element. If the array is already at capacity the element\nis not stored, the size is left unchanged and err is set to ERROR_VALIDATION . On success err is left untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_dp_t ), intent(inout) :: self real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: value type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private pure subroutine fixed_array_int_at (self, index, value, err) Bounds-checked element access, 1-based. Any index outside 1:size() (including indices that are within the capacity but\nbeyond the live elements) sets value to zero and err to ERROR_VALIDATION . On success err is left untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(in) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: index integer(kind=default_int), intent(out) :: value type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private pure subroutine fixed_array_int_clear (self) Drop every element. The storage itself is untouched, so this is a\nsingle integer assignment; the array can be reused immediately. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(inout) :: self private pure subroutine fixed_array_int_pop_back (self, value, err) Remove and return the last element (LIFO). On an empty array value is set to zero and err is set to ERROR_VALIDATION .\nOn success err is left untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(out) :: value type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err private pure subroutine fixed_array_int_push_back (self, value, err) Append an element. If the array is already at capacity the element\nis not stored, the size is left unchanged and err is set to ERROR_VALIDATION . On success err is left untouched. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( fixed_array_int_t ), intent(inout) :: self integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: value type( error_t ), intent(inout) :: err","tags":"","url":"module/pic_fixed_array.html"},{"title":"pic_statistics – PIC","text":"This module provides simple reductions over rank-1 arrays. To avoid\nprecision loss and integer overflow, mean , variance and std_dev always accumulate in and return real(dp), regardless of the input type. min_max preserves the input type and returns the two extremes in a\nlength-2 array. Uses pic_types module~~pic_statistics~~UsesGraph module~pic_statistics pic_statistics module~pic_types pic_types module~pic_statistics->module~pic_types iso_c_binding iso_c_binding module~pic_types->iso_c_binding iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~pic_types->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Interfaces public        interface mean Arithmetic mean of a 1-D array, returned as real(dp). Returns 0 for an empty array. Supported input types are:\ninteger(int32), integer(int64), real(sp), real(dp).\nUsage: m = mean(array) private pure function mean_int32 (array) result(m) Mean of an integer(int32) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function mean_int64 (array) result(m) Mean of an integer(int64) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function mean_sp (array) result(m) Mean of a real(sp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function mean_dp (array) result(m) Mean of a real(dp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=dp) public        interface min_max Minimum and maximum of a 1-D array in a single length-2 result. Returns [minval(array), maxval(array)] , preserving the input type.\nThe result is undefined for an empty array. Supported types are:\ninteger(int32), integer(int64), real(sp), real(dp).\nUsage: mm = min_max(array)  ! mm(1) = min, mm(2) = max private pure function min_max_int32 (array) result(mm) Minimum and maximum of an integer(int32) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value integer(kind=int32), (2) private pure function min_max_int64 (array) result(mm) Minimum and maximum of an integer(int64) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value integer(kind=int64), (2) private pure function min_max_sp (array) result(mm) Minimum and maximum of a real(sp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=sp), (2) private pure function min_max_dp (array) result(mm) Minimum and maximum of a real(dp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=dp), (2) public        interface std_dev Standard deviation of a 1-D array, returned as real(dp). Equal to sqrt(variance(array, sample)) ; see variance for the meaning\nof the optional sample flag.\nUsage: s = std_dev(array [, sample]) private pure function std_dev_int32 (array, sample) result(s) Standard deviation of an integer(int32) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function std_dev_int64 (array, sample) result(s) Standard deviation of an integer(int64) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function std_dev_sp (array, sample) result(s) Standard deviation of a real(sp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function std_dev_dp (array, sample) result(s) Standard deviation of a real(dp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) public        interface variance Variance of a 1-D array, returned as real(dp). By default the unbiased sample variance (dividing by n - 1 ) is\nreturned; pass sample = .false. for the population variance (dividing\nby n ). Returns 0 when there are too few elements to define it.\nSupported input types are: integer(int32), integer(int64), real(sp),\nreal(dp).\nUsage: v = variance(array [, sample]) private pure function variance_int32 (array, sample) result(v) Variance of an integer(int32) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function variance_int64 (array, sample) result(v) Variance of an integer(int64) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=int64), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function variance_sp (array, sample) result(v) Variance of a real(sp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=sp), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function variance_dp (array, sample) result(v) Variance of a real(dp) array (core implementation, two-pass). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: array (:) logical, intent(in), optional :: sample Return Value real(kind=dp) Functions private pure function mean_dp (array) result(m) Mean of a real(dp) array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name real(kind=dp), intent(in) :: array (:) Return Value real(kind=dp) private pure function mean_int32 (array) result(m) Mean of an integer(int32) array. Arguments Type Intent Opti