 Attributes Name class( frame_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private  function frame_render (this) result(output) The escape sequence that brings the screen up to date. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( frame_t ), intent(inout) :: this Return Value character(len=:), allocatable private pure function frame_row_count (this) result(r) Number of lines the frame holds. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( frame_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value integer(kind=default_int) private pure function pending_is_empty (this) result(r) Whether a partial sequence is being carried. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( pending_t ), intent(in) :: this Return Value logical Subroutines public pure subroutine decode_keys (pending, bytes, events, n_events) Decode raw terminal bytes into key events. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( pending_t ), intent(inout) :: pending Carried partial sequence; pass the same one every call. character(len=*), intent(in) :: bytes Bytes just read from the terminal. May be empty, which is how a\ncaller flushes a held ESC . type( key_event_t ), intent(out) :: events (:) Decoded events, filled from 1. integer(kind=default_int), intent(out) :: n_events How many entries of events were filled. private pure subroutine decode_single (byte, event) Decode one byte that is not part of an escape sequence. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: byte iachar value of the byte. type( key_event_t ), intent(out) :: event private pure subroutine emit (events, n_events, code, char_code) Append an event, silently dropping any beyond the caller’s array. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( key_event_t ), intent(inout) :: events (:) integer(kind=default_int), intent(inout) :: n_events integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: code integer(kind=int32), intent(in) :: char_code private  subroutine frame_invalidate (this) Force the next render to emit every row. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( frame_t ), intent(inout) :: this private  subroutine frame_resize (this, rows, cols) Set the frame’s dimensions, discarding the diff. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( frame_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: rows Number of lines; below 0 is treated as 0. integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: cols Width in code points; below 0 is treated as 0. private  subroutine frame_set_line (this, row, text) Set one line, truncated to the frame width in code points. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( frame_t ), intent(inout) :: this integer(kind=default_int), intent(in) :: row One-based row. character(len=*), intent(in) :: text Text for the row. private pure subroutine match_sequence (seq, complete, event, consumed) Test whether seq is a finished escape sequence. Read more… Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: seq Bytes accumulated so far, starting with ESC. logical, intent(out) :: complete Whether a decision has been reached. type( key_event_t ), intent(out) :: event The decoded key, or KEY_NONE if the sequence is unknown. integer(kind=default_int), intent(out) :: consumed How many leading bytes of seq the decision used. private pure subroutine pending_clear (this) Forget any partial escape sequence. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name class( pending_t ), intent(inout) :: this","tags":"","url":"module/pic_ansi.html"},{"title":"pic_sorting_radix_sort – PIC","text":"The generic subroutine implementing the LSD radix sort algorithm to return\n an input array with its elements sorted in order of (non-)decreasing\n value. Its use has the syntax: call radix_sort( array[, work, reverse] ) with the arguments: array: the rank 1 array to be sorted. It is an intent(inout) argument of any of the types integer(int8) , integer(int16) , integer(int32) , integer(int64) , real(real32) , real(real64) .\n   If both the type of array is real and at least one of the\n   elements is a NaN , then the ordering of the result is undefined.\n   Otherwise it is defined to be the original elements in\n   non-decreasing order. Especially, -0.0 is lesser than 0.0. work (optional): shall be a rank 1 array of the same type as array , and shall have at least size(array) elements. It is an intent(inout) argument to be used as buffer. Its value on return is\n   undefined. If it is not present, radix_sort will allocate a\n   buffer for use, and deallocate it before return. If you do several\n   similar radix_sort s, reusing the work array is a good parctice.\n   This argument is not present for int8_radix_sort because it use\n   counting sort, so no buffer is needed. reverse (optional): shall be a scalar of type default logical. It\n   is an intent(in) argument. If present with a value of .true. then array will be sorted in order of non-increasing values in stable\n   order. Otherwise index will sort array in order of non-decreasing\n   values in stable order. Example ... ! Read random data from a file call read_file ( 'dummy_file' , array ) ! Sort the random data call radix_sort ( array ) ... Uses pic_error Ancestors: pic_sorting module~~pic_sorting_radix_sort~~UsesGraph module~pic_sorting_radix_sort pic_sorting_radix_sort module~pic_error pic_error module~pic_sorting_radix_sort->module~pic_error module~pic_sorting pic_sorting module~pic_sorting_radix_sort->module~pic_sorting module~pic_global_definitions pic_global_definitions module~pic_error->module~pic_global_definitions module~pic_types pic_types module~pic_error->module~pic_types module~pic_sorting->module~pic_error module~pic_optional_value pic_optional_value module~pic_sorting->module~pic_optional_value module~pic_sorting->module~pic_types module~pic_global_definitions->module~pic_types module~pic_optional_value->module~pic_types iso_c_binding 